## Resolved mutable: m-3001-8090-render-identical-scripted

RESOLVED + true cause found. :3001 and :8090 render IDENTICALLY at every scripted camera (browser-110 orbit 429/429 both; browser-113 identical-framing pixel-identical; browser-114 hands-off 69/69 both) -- the port is NOT the variable. The REAL bug (browser-115, live spawn camera): 2 clusters have on-screen geometry but are NOT drawn (onScreen 56, drawn 54, wrongCull 2). The wrongly-culled clusters are THIN FLAT SLABS (size 2.9x0.2x0.7, 1.7x0.1x1.7 -- 0.1-0.2m thick floor/panel pieces). A thin slab's bounding SPHERE is small + centered, so when the camera is close the sphere falls outside the frustum while the slab's broad face is still on-screen -> false cull. As the camera rotates different thin slabs flip in/out = 'parts appear/disappear on camera move'. Per-cluster sphere-cull under-covers thin geometry. Fix: disable per-cluster frustum cull for the always-near env cluster mesh (whole arena small + always near; like player VRM frustumCulled=false).